# **Without this file the image ships the build on the developer's disk** (the
# readiness audit of 2026-09-28). `deploy/Dockerfile` copies `packages`, `apps/api`
# and `tools/sim` and then runs `npm run build`, which is `tsc -b`: with a
# `.tsbuildinfo` and a `dist/` from the host in the context, every project reads as
# up to date and nothing is emitted, so `CMD node apps/api/dist/main.js` runs
# JavaScript compiled from another tree — possibly another commit — with no signal
# that it did. The guide already warns about this for a hand copy
# (`INTEGRATION.md`: delete the `*.tsbuildinfo` before building elsewhere); the
# image needs the same thing, and a build context is where it can be enforced.
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/node_modules
.git
.github
**/coverage
apps/web/.next
apps/web/.next-stat
.otc-state
**/.otc-state
*.log
